The scene is quite dark and the characters look small at distance. We teleported to DARA at (-13,21.2) but camera is still far from previous state or yaw different. I see multiple NPCs in a row (we placed NPCs along x -15..12 at z~18-25, Sable, Dara, etc.) — they are visible. They look humanoid with heads and limbs. The cat is visible in foreground right, nicely modeled (visible ears, tail, eyes?). It looks good.

But close-up camera isn't close. Again camera lerp slow due to frames. Need to verify NPC details with fixed camera via debug: set camera.position directly and lookAt after teleport, but updateCamera overrides each frame. Could add debug function to freeze camera. Or take screenshot immediately after teleport with camera snapped? Camera lerp over frames.

To validate details, set `pitch` low and `yaw` toward NPC, then teleport close; camera converges. We can modify debug to expose `snapCamera` or an override. Since updateCamera overrides, use a flag `window.__freezeCam` checked in updateCamera (temporary). Simpler: add `window.__dbg.freezeCamera(pos,target)` that sets `camera.position` and `camera.lookAt`, plus a global `cameraOverride=true`; in updateCamera, if override, return. Add temporary. But we'll remove hook later anyway.

Alternatively, reason that character geometry is correct; but visual check important to catch glaring issues (e.g., eyes on back, hair covering face). Let me add a temporary freeze via `window.__freeze` boolean in updateCamera:
```js
if(window.__freeze) return;
```
Then debug sets camera position and lookAt each test. We'll remove the flag at the end.

Also fix interior wall fade.

Let's edit wallMat storage + fade + freeze.

In buildEnterableBuilding:
```js
const built={x,z,w,d,h,name:o.sign.text,wallMat};interiors.push(built)
```
wallMat already const. Good.

In updateCamera:
```js
let activeRoom=null;
...
const room=interiorAt(...);
if(room!==activeRoom){
 if(activeRoom){activeRoom.wallMat.opacity=1;activeRoom.wallMat.transparent=false;activeRoom.wallMat.depthWrite=true;activeRoom.wallMat.needsUpdate=true}
 if(room){room.wallMat.opacity=.2;room.wallMat.transparent=true;room.wallMat.depthWrite=false;room.wallMat.needsUpdate=true}
 activeRoom=room;
}
if(window.__freeze)return;
```
But updateCamera called before updateWorld each frame; activeRoom state maintained. Need `let activeRoom=null` near function.

Potential issue: wallMat may be shared with other meshes within the same building only. Fine.

Also material transparent toggling requires needsUpdate? Changing transparent may require `needsUpdate=true` for program? In three, transparent affects render list but not shader; no needsUpdate needed but safe.

Now freeze. Add to updateCamera after room handling:
```js
if(window.__freezeCamera)return;
```

Let's patch.

